    midout wide: phase-2 stores at W 64 rotated over the four tasks' chunks
    
    In the digit-major layout a chunk is one bank pair, so a task's store
    (one chunk, lane = digit) put all 64 lanes on one pair. The four
    tasks' words are now kept and stored afterwards, lane l taking task
    (l + j) & 3 in store j: four chunks per store. The words stored and
    their places are the same. Phase 3b forms each chunk's row index as
    digit * 32 + the chunk's word offset.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

